    "transcript": {
        "duration": 62.20000076293945,
        "text": "How do you get the actual key and voice? You go to 11Labs. If you don't have an account, you need to register. I'll leave a link in the description. You log in and you'll be on something like this. You'll need to go to the developers, click here where it says API keys, create a new API key, and then you need to click this one, at least, and you create a key, and then you just copy the result you get in this first step. Then you need an actual voice, so for the actual voice you need to go to the voices, and then you can filter whatever you want. For example, if I select English, let's say English, let's say the accent we want is American, and let's say we want narration. So we have a bunch of voices which you can play. that sadness and joy can coexist so compatibly with one another",
